WEBVTT

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:08.570
This is Hotsauce, a free, open source office suite for small teams,

00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:10.870
running on your own server.

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:12.910
Here's a quick look at each app.

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:16.910
The day starts on Today: your meetings, your tasks,

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:19.950
and what changed since yesterday, on one page.

00:00:22.184 --> 00:00:26.924
Docs are plain Markdown files, kept in Git.

00:00:26.924 --> 00:00:29.004
Link docs with two square brackets,

00:00:29.004 --> 00:00:33.684
and step back through every version to see who changed what.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:40.640
Meetings takes the notes for you, and no bot joins your call.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:44.600
Your rough notes and the transcript become clean notes,

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:47.520
with decisions and action items.

00:00:48.149 --> 00:00:52.049
Ask a question across every meeting and doc,

00:00:52.049 --> 00:00:56.109
and the answer points back to its sources.

00:00:56.109 --> 00:00:58.469
Hotsauce also writes a brief,

00:00:58.469 --> 00:01:02.449
so your AI agents already know what you're working on.

00:01:04.729 --> 00:01:08.249
Action items land in Tasks.

00:01:08.249 --> 00:01:12.969
Type one in plain words, or just ramble for a few seconds,

00:01:12.969 --> 00:01:16.409
and Hotsauce sorts it into a clean list.

00:01:19.896 --> 00:01:22.936
Notes hold the small stuff.

00:01:22.936 --> 00:01:27.256
Color them, pin them, or turn them into checklists.

00:01:30.829 --> 00:01:33.369
Check-ins ask the team a question on a schedule,

00:01:33.369 --> 00:01:36.669
like what will you get done this week,

00:01:36.669 --> 00:01:39.989
and gather everyone's answers in one place.

00:01:43.562 --> 00:01:46.982
Clips replaces the meeting you didn't need.

00:01:46.982 --> 00:01:49.382
Record your screen and talk it through.

00:01:49.382 --> 00:01:52.762
Whoever watches gets a transcript and a summary.

00:01:54.575 --> 00:01:58.755
Dictate turns talking into clean text.

00:01:58.755 --> 00:02:01.855
Hold a key on your Mac and speak into any app,

00:02:01.855 --> 00:02:04.695
or leave a voice note from your phone.

00:02:05.175 --> 00:02:09.175
The Mac app sets itself up one step at a time.

00:02:09.175 --> 00:02:12.375
Enter your team's workspace, and sign in with Google,

00:02:12.375 --> 00:02:14.875
which connects Dictate too.

00:02:14.875 --> 00:02:18.455
Try it in the practice box, then see each permission it needs,

00:02:18.455 --> 00:02:21.875
with a plain reason for every one.

00:02:21.875 --> 00:02:24.195
Skip one, and it asks again later.

00:02:25.782 --> 00:02:28.842
Found a bug, or have an idea?

00:02:28.842 --> 00:02:31.442
Send feedback from any page.

00:02:31.442 --> 00:02:34.142
Attach a picture of the page you were on with one click,

00:02:34.142 --> 00:02:36.562
then follow what happens to it.

00:02:39.072 --> 00:02:44.072
And there's more: whiteboards for sketching ideas together,

00:02:44.072 --> 00:02:49.092
a people directory, shared files, forms, and Briefcast,

00:02:49.092 --> 00:02:52.012
a morning briefing you can play like a podcast.

00:02:52.777 --> 00:02:59.117
Hotsauce is free and open source, and it deploys to Cloudflare in minutes.

00:02:59.117 --> 00:03:01.617
Get it at hotsauce.work.
